# What restore-home.sh copies back into /home/<user>. Everything else stays in the backup (borg,
# restic, or the pre-reinstall NAS copy) and can be pulled from there by hand.
# One path per line, relative to the home folder; a folder brings everything under it.
# `OLD => NEW` copies OLD to NEW instead: apps that moved to Flatpak read their XDG dirs from
# ~/.var/app/<id>/{config,data}. Flatpaks with home access may keep using the host path (DBeaver
# does), so check where the Flatpak actually writes before adding a remap.
# ~/.var/app/<id> is restored for every app in flatpaks.txt (minus cache/), no need to list them.

